    {
      "id": "claim_c40b8337230943bea1f39a5dbb15a9ee",
      "statement": "The Hub exposes a single WebSocket route, /ws, whose handler (Server.handleWS) branches on the first received proto.Message: Role \"ui\" registers a browser tab as a uiConn and replays a state/PTY-output snapshot before entering a per-connection UI read loop, Type \"register\" creates a new session record and enters wrapperLoop, and Type \"reattach\" reconnects to an existing session via reattachLoop instead of creating a duplicate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/server.go#L1856-L1936",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d50fe0877b1518c15dfe3611e918c7d3e35b69fa9714a6ee1e24cf7e8a6ebc7c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_85a9242e23ec4b4b8c5a7fcfff626e9e",
      "statement": "Every /ws connection, whether UI or wrapper role, is authenticated before role-specific logic runs: it must present a valid token or qualify for the hub.allow_loopback_without_token exception, and if remote-PIN protection applies to the caller, a valid PIN cookie is also required.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/server.go#L1863-L1879",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fdd0e267eea7f70a5609418885a1b48e95d29863220386ea9903dbe5cb544430:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cecae3821aea4d11b386942ddfd71d57",
      "statement": "internal/wrapper's ensureHub skips probing for or starting a Hub entirely when MANY_AI_CLI=1 is set in its own environment (meaning it was itself spawned by a Hub), because starting a second Hub in that situation risks killing the real Hub via a stale PID file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/wrapper/wrapper.go#L1677-L1694",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:73afb42c7eb202db3d9115cabc53170506bb727b5d3aa290d77c15a0bd3b9c9c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_41d19ed89d9e4108bfed56d342d0bb45",
      "statement": "When ensureHub finds no reachable Hub on the configured port, it selects a free port near the configured one via findFreePort, launches `many-ai-cli serve --port <port>` as a detached child process, and waits up to a fixed timeout for it to become ready before the wrap continues, killing the spawned process if it does not become ready in time.",
      "evidence": [
